  "_comment": [
    "Named places on Chernarus, as world coordinates in metres.",
    "",
    "These are FACTS about the game world - where Bohemia put a village - written down here so",
    "the map can label itself. They are not copied from anyone's drawing of the map.",
    "",
    "Accuracy: read off a 1 km grid and cross-checked against the fixture towns in",
    "test/demo.js, which disagree by up to about half a kilometre, mostly northward. So treat",
    "every position here as good to roughly 500 m and no better. The building layer underneath",
    "is built from the mission's own mapgrouppos.xml and is the thing to trust when the two",
    "disagree: switch the basemap layer on, see which way a label sits off its cluster, and",
    "nudge the numbers here until it lands. Nothing else needs changing.",
    "",
    "class decides when a label appears as you zoom: city and town always, the rest once there",
    "is room. Add your own line and it shows up on the next reload - nothing else to change.",
    "",
    "The far north of the map is thin here on purpose. The reference used to place these did not",
    "name Severograd, Tisy, Novaya Petrovka or the other northern settlements, and a guess is",
    "worse than a gap. Add them if you know them."
  ],
